course: dictionary
lesson: 16018
title: Strong feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vehemently is an adverb. It tells you how something is done, and here it shows that the feeling is very strong. «"I did not break the vase!" Mia said vehemently.» Mia is not just saying no. She says it with great force, and she really means it.
explain: Look at the words around vehemently for clues. It often comes after words like deny, oppose or argue, because people show strong feeling when they disagree. «The mayor vehemently opposed the new road.» The word opposed tells you the mayor was against it, and vehemently shows how strongly.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say «She said it with very strong feeling» instead? Yes, so vehemently means with very strong feeling, especially when disagreeing or denying something.
fact: Vehemently is an adverb, so it describes how an action is done.
fact: Vehemently means with very strong feeling.
fact: It is often used when someone disagrees with something or denies it.
fact: Common phrases are «vehemently deny» and «vehemently oppose».
fact: The related adjective is vehement, as in a vehement denial: a very strong denial.
exercise: «"I never touched your bike!" Sam said vehemently.» What does vehemently mean here? | Without any feeling at all | With a quiet, shy voice | With a big smile | *With very strong feeling
exercise: «The team vehemently opposed the change to the rules.» Find the word that tells you how strongly the team felt. | team | *vehemently | change
exercise: Which meaning fits vehemently best? | Very slowly | *With very strong feeling | Quietly and calmly | With a happy smile
test: «The mayor vehemently opposed the plan to close the park.» What does vehemently tell us? | *The mayor felt very strongly against the plan | Only a little bit | The mayor was asleep | The mayor was happy about the plan
test: «We did not cheat!» the twins said vehemently. Why would they say it vehemently? | They wanted a snack | They were lost | *They felt very strongly that it was not true | They were bored
exam: Which sentence uses vehemently correctly? | The baby slept vehemently all night | The rain fell vehemently because it was sunny | She ate her soup vehemently and quietly | *The witness vehemently denied taking the money
